@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: how a published CLI release is resolved, verified and installed over the CDN
' covers: internal/cdn/**
' covers: cmd/proveo/update.go
' covers: apps/cli/public/cli/**
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/stagecdn.go
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/buildcli.go
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/deploycli.go
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/devcli.go
'
' ── MAINTAINER RELEASE PATH: cmd/proveo-dev (not shipped) ──────────────────
' `proveo-dev stage-cdn` replaced scripts/stage-cli-cdn.sh, and
' `proveo-dev build-cli|deploy-cli|dev-cli` replaced the mise task bodies
' (host-shell-to-go P4). goreleaser lists its binaries explicitly and
' proveo-dev is not among them, so it never reaches the CDN.
' * stage-cdn sources each proveo-<goos>-<goarch>[.exe] from dist/ in order:
'   proveo_*_<os>_<arch>.{tar.gz,tgz,zip}, the flat cdn-proveo archive, then
'   raw goreleaser build dirs. It cross-compiles only when none exists, and
'   PROVEO_CDN_REQUIRE_DIST=1 (set by build-cli --release) turns that fallback
'   into a failure, so a release never ships a dev cross-build.
' * Version precedence: PROVEO_VERSION, dist/artifacts.json, dist/VERSION,
'   git describe (exact tag, then --always), "dev".
' * It first deletes the legacy bash consumer assets (bin/proveo, help.sh,
'   init.sh, lib/) and every stale proveo-* asset, so the tree carries exactly
'   what latest.json lists.
' * build-cli installs into $(go env GOPATH)/bin, not a toolchain-local GOBIN
'   that mise may set. It stamps dev@<short-sha> so a stale binary is visible
'   in `proveo --version`.
' * goreleaser is pinned (v2.17.0) when build-cli installs it, so release
'   builds are reproducible; bump it deliberately.
' covers: internal/installtest/**
' covers: internal/contract/installer_bash_test.go
'
' ── THE INSTALL SUITE RUNS THE INTERPRETER USERS GET ───────────────────────
' internal/installtest executes the real install.sh / uninstall.sh. On darwin
' it invokes /bin/bash explicitly: the scripts' `#!/usr/bin/env bash` resolves
' to a Homebrew bash 5 on a maintainer Mac, which hides every 3.2 breaker that
' `curl … | bash` meets on a stock Mac. Elsewhere it takes bash from PATH.
'
' It stages its own CDN (go build ./cmd/proveo + checksums.txt + latest.json)
' so it stays hermetic and runs in the default test lane. PROVEO_INSTALLTEST_CDN
' points it at an already staged tree instead, to verify the release stage.
'
' The bootstrap cases serve a STUB proveo that records its argv. install.sh
' runs `proveo init` after placing the binary, and the real one reaches GitHub
' and installs sbx: a hundred-megabyte download inside a unit suite, on
' whatever host runs it.
'
' Inherited PROVEO_* variables are dropped from every child: a PROVEO_VERSION
' or PROVEO_SKIP_INIT in the operator's shell would otherwise steer the cases.
' internal/contract/installer_bash_test.go guards the same scripts statically
' (`/bin/bash -n`, bash-4-only syntax, unguarded "${arr[@]}" under set -u).

title Distribution + self-update — install.sh and `proveo update`

actor "Consumer" as USER

node "Maintainer host" as MH <<host>> {
  component "goreleaser\nmulti-arch static binaries" as GR <<app>>
  component "proveo-dev stage-cdn\nstages apps/cli/public/cli" as STAGE <<app>>
}

cloud "Cloudflare — proveo.ca/cli" as CDN <<cloud>> {
  artifact "latest.json\n{version, checksums{basename→sha256}, base_url}" as MANIFEST <<db>>
  artifact "proveo-<goos>-<goarch>[.exe]" as ASSET <<db>>
}

node "Consumer host" as CH <<host>> {
  component "dist/install.sh · install.ps1" as INSTALL <<app>>
  component "cmd/proveo update\n--check | --force" as UPD <<app>>
  component "internal/cdn\nBaseURL · FetchManifest\nCurrentAssetName · Newer\nDownloadAsset · IsDevVersion" as CDNPKG <<app>>
  component "proveo binary on PATH" as BIN <<app>>
  component "cmd/proveo setup\nPATH via internal/shell" as SETUP <<app>>
}

GR ARROW_MAIN STAGE
STAGE ARROW_CLOUD CDN : wrangler deploy
USER ARROW_MAIN INSTALL
INSTALL ARROW_CLOUD MANIFEST : fetch
INSTALL ARROW_CLOUD ASSET : download
INSTALL ARROW_MAIN BIN : install + successLabel(sha256 verified)
INSTALL ARROW_OPTIONAL SETUP : hand off PATH wiring

USER ARROW_MAIN UPD
UPD ARROW_MAIN CDNPKG
CDNPKG ARROW_CLOUD MANIFEST : " ""FetchManifest(client, BaseURL())"" "
CDNPKG ARROW_MAIN CDNPKG : " ""Newer(remote, local)"" "
CDNPKG ARROW_CLOUD ASSET : " ""DownloadAsset(…, wantHex)"" "
CDNPKG ARROW_ERROR BIN : errorLabel(checksum mismatch → abort)
CDNPKG ARROW_MAIN BIN : atomic replace

note right of CDNPKG
  **Checksum is the trust root.** The asset is only
  installed when its sha256 matches the ""checksums""
  entry in ""latest.json""; a mismatch aborts without
  touching the installed binary. The manifest may
  redirect downloads via its own ""base_url"".

  ""AssetName(goos, goarch)"" is the naming contract
  shared by goreleaser, the staged CDN tree and the
  updater — they must agree or every update 404s.

  A dev build (""IsDevVersion"", e.g. ""dev@<sha>"") is
  never auto-replaced unless ""--force"" is passed, so a
  locally built binary is not clobbered by a release.
end note

note bottom of CDN
  Release assets only — no application code runs here.
  Publishing: an exact git tag builds semver artifacts
  (no GitHub Release); otherwise ""--snapshot"".
end note
note bottom of MANIFEST
  **One published channel, so a pinned version is not a time machine.** The
  installers read the version from ""latest\.json"" unless ""PROVEO_VERSION"" is
  set, and an explicit value must match what the CDN currently publishes — the
  bucket carries the current release only, so pinning an older tag resolves to
  nothing rather than to that older build.
end note

@enduml
